      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do you do the plumbing, tiling and fitting?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. We handle everything with our own employed team. Plumbing by Gas Safe registered engineers, tiling by employed tilers, and all fitting in-house. No sub-contractors. One team. One schedule. One point of contact. This is the single biggest reason Liverpool homeowners choose us over competitors who only handle the plumbing and leave you to find a separate tiler." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can you design a bathroom for me?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Every project starts with a free design consultation. We discuss your taste, scour Pinterest boards together, look at tile samples and produce a full specification with mood board before any quote is finalised. The design service is included at no extra cost when you proceed with the installation." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can you fit a bathroom in a Liverpool Victorian property?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Liverpool's Victorian and Edwardian housing stock is our specialism. These properties often have narrow bathroom footprints, unusual layouts, original cast iron waste pipes and solid walls. We design the bathroom around the specific characteristics of your property and preserve period features wherever possible. Wide-plank tiling, freestanding baths and period-appropriate brassware suit these homes particularly well." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Will a new bathroom add value to my Liverpool property?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. A premium, well-designed bathroom can increase Liverpool property value by 4 to 6% according to recent estate agent surveys. On a property worth £250,000 that is a £10,000-£15,000 uplift. More importantly, a premium bathroom removes the most common pre-exchange objection from buyers and shortens time-to-sale. We offer free design consultations for Liverpool homeowners renovating before listing." } },
