  <!-- OUR APPROACH -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Our Design-Led Approach to Bathroom Fitting in Liverpool</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We believe a bathroom should be beautiful, restorative and built to last. Three principles guide every project.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>1. Pinterest research, weekly</strong><p>We scour Pinterest and design publications weekly to spot emerging trends before they hit the mainstream. We share mood boards with you at the design consultation so you can see what's working in 2026 bathrooms globally, not just what was popular five years ago. Your Liverpool bathroom should feel current the day it's finished.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>2. Premium materials only</strong><p>We specify Villeroy & Boch, Duravit, Geberit, Crosswater, Hansgrohe, Grohe, Lusso Stone and BC Designs as standard. Tiles from premium UK and Italian suppliers. Brassware that retains its finish for decades, not the chrome-plated zinc that yellows after two years. The cheapest part of your bathroom is usually the labour. The materials are what last.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>3. Timeless over trendy</strong><p>The best 2026 bathrooms borrow from current design language without becoming dated by 2030. We help you distinguish between trends worth chasing (microcement, freestanding baths, sculptural lighting) and trends that will date your bathroom in 18 months (bold neon tiles, ultra-shiny gold everything, novelty shapes). Your bathroom should feel just as beautiful in 2046 as it does on completion day.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>One team for everything</strong><p>Plumbing, tiling and fitting all by our own employed staff. No sub-contractors. The Gas Safe registered engineer plumbing your bathroom on Monday is the same person tiling on Wednesday. One schedule. One point of contact. One invoice. No gaps and no finger-pointing between trades when issues arise.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PREMIUM BRANDS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Premium Brands We Install in Liverpool Bathrooms</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We work with UK and European premium manufacturers. The names below are not aspirational, they are our standard specification.</p>

      <div class="pf-why-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Villeroy & Boch</h3>
          <p>German premium ceramics. The Subway and Memento ranges are particularly suited to Liverpool's mid-to-large bathrooms. Their ceramic glaze finish resists limescale build-up significantly better than budget brands, which matters in Merseyside's hard water area.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Duravit</h3>
          <p>German contemporary design. The Starck and ME by Starck ranges deliver clean architectural lines suited to modern Liverpool apartments. Strong warranties and replacement parts available for decades.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Geberit</h3>
          <p>The standard for concealed cisterns and wall-hung toilet frames. We use Geberit Duofix frames as standard for any wall-hung toilet installation. Their AquaClean shower toilet range is increasingly requested in Liverpool master en suites.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Hansgrohe</h3>
          <p>Premium German showering. The AXOR and Hansgrohe Raindance ranges deliver shower experiences that justify their price tag. PVD coatings on their chrome and brass finishes resist tarnishing. We specify Hansgrohe for any shower installation where performance and longevity matter.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Grohe</h3>
          <p>The reliable workhorse of premium brassware. Strong UK availability for parts and consistent quality across their range. We specify Grohe basin and bath taps in many Liverpool bathrooms where understated quality is the goal.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Crosswater</h3>
          <p>UK premium designer. Particularly strong on contemporary brassware in non-chrome finishes. Brushed brass, matte black and gunmetal options for Liverpool bathrooms looking for something more distinctive than chrome.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-who-item">
          <h3>Lusso Stone</h3>
          <p>UK luxury bathroom specialist. Solid stone basins, freestanding stone baths and statement vanities for Liverpool master bathrooms where the bathroom is a feature room. Higher specification, longer lead times, but utterly distinctive.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>BC Designs</h3>
          <p>UK manufacturer of premium freestanding baths and basins. Their copper and cast iron finishes work beautifully in Liverpool's Victorian and Edwardian properties. Substantial pieces designed to be a focal point.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-alert" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <strong>Why we don't fit budget brands</strong>
        <p>The bathroom industry is full of budget products that look identical to premium brands in the showroom but degrade within 2 to 5 years. Chrome plating peels. Cartridges fail. Ceramics craze and stain. Replacing a budget brassware set in 3 years costs as much as fitting premium brassware from day one, and you've lived with disappointing performance the whole time. We only install brands with verified long-term performance records.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2026 TRENDS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>2026 Bathroom Trends in Liverpool Homes</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">These are the design directions defining luxury bathrooms in 2026, and how we're applying them to Liverpool's housing stock. Some are timeless additions. Others are calculated trend choices. We help you decide which is which at the design consultation.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Microcement seamless surfaces</strong><p>Hand-applied, ultra-thin cement finish creating a grout-free seamless surface across walls and floors. The look of polished concrete without the construction work. Particularly striking in Liverpool's contemporary apartments and converted spaces. Requires specialist application but delivers a finish nothing else can match.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Sculptural freestanding baths</strong><p>The freestanding bath has shifted from period reproduction to architectural sculpture. Stone resin, copper-finish and cast iron baths in clean modern shapes. We specify BC Designs and Lusso Stone for Liverpool homes where the bath is the centrepiece of the bathroom. Best positioned beneath a window or centrally placed in larger Liverpool master bathrooms.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Curbless and doorless walk-in showers</strong><p>The 2026 shower has no shower tray and no door. The floor tile runs uninterrupted from dry zone to wet zone with a linear drain. Visually expansive, easier to clean and inherently accessible. Requires full tanking and precise floor falls, which is why most bathroom fitters won't quote them properly. We install dozens across Liverpool every year.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Old-world wallpapered bathrooms</strong><p>Bathroom wallpaper is back, but the 2026 take is ornate and pattern-heavy. Botanicals, toiles, damasks and oversized florals on a single feature wall or above tiled wainscoting. Particularly beautiful in Liverpool's Victorian properties where the pattern complements original cornicing and skirtings.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Sculptural statement lighting</strong><p>Pendants and lanterns are migrating from living rooms into bathrooms. Cloud-form pendants, pleated lantern fixtures and oversized statement lighting that soften the hard edges of tile and stone. Requires correct IP-rated specification for bathroom zones, which we handle as standard.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Hand-painted artisanal tiles</strong><p>Mass-produced graphic tiles are giving way to hand-painted Delft-style, soft floral and irregular-brushstroke tiles. Particularly suited to small Liverpool en suites and cloakrooms where one wall can become a statement feature without overwhelming the space.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Mixed-metal finishes</strong><p>The matchy-matchy bathroom is over. 2026 bathrooms combine brushed brass taps with matte black hardware and chrome accents in considered combinations. We help you specify mixed metals at the design consultation so the result looks intentional rather than accidental.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Floating vanities</strong><p>Wall-hung vanity units with the floor running underneath visually expand the bathroom and make cleaning effortless. Particularly effective in Liverpool's smaller second bathrooms and en suites where floor space is limited. Requires wall blocking at first-fix stage, which is why retrofitting them later usually fails.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Underfloor heating</strong><p>No longer a luxury. Electric underfloor heating is now standard specification in premium Liverpool bathrooms. The cost premium over a traditional radiator is modest, and the comfort benefit is transformative. We install it as default in all supply and fit bathrooms above £7,000.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Spa-like and tech-free</strong><p>Counter to the smart-bathroom hype, 2026's design direction is calmer. Soft lighting, natural materials, somewhere to sit, no screens. The bathroom as the one room in the house that helps you disconnect. We design around this principle when clients want a restorative bathroom rather than a tech showcase.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-orange" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3>Trend choices we'd advise against</h3>
        <p>Not every 2026 trend deserves your money. We'd steer Liverpool homeowners away from extreme dopamine-coloured fixtures (bubblegum pink toilets date faster than any other choice), heavily themed mosaic feature walls, and over-engineered smart-mirror installations where the technology will be obsolete before the bathroom needs refurbishing again. The best bathrooms balance current design language with materials and forms that won't feel dated in five years.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

